From 4991db38d76a20ff84282cc965019fcb501529d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:51:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Map growth: ExtendFrontier raises the outermost ring up to a
 season ceiling

Adds `r_max_ceiling` to the conquest block (offset 78; 0 = r_max is final,
as before) and `r_max_ext` to the Frontier (offset 66, formerly reserve).
A new class-D instruction ExtendFrontier (v2 0xC1) raises the effective
outermost ring by one when every ring up to it is open, a bell has passed
since the last opening and some wedge is at the theta occupancy, the same
conditions as OpenRing; the new ring is then opened by OpenRing as any
other. Within the ceiling only: this is a bounded extension path (hard
maximum ring 128), not an unbounded map.

- program: `effective_r_max` in OpenRing, FileTicket, FileOutpost and
  PlaceHome; OpenProvince checks the ceiling and relies on the RingSeed.
  Log FRONTIER_EXTENDED (Frontier).
- herald: `/h/world` rMax is the effective value; the fold accepts the new
  record kind. fclient: builder, decode of r_max_ext, land bounds.
- tests: LiteSVM `tests/map_extend.rs` (refused without a ceiling; grows
  one ring; old terrain byte-identical; repeated extension and province
  creation refused; outpost from ring 2 into the new ring 5), coverage
  table, preset validation, node world test; ABI vectors and generated
  web SDK regenerated.

The conquest block layout (placement at 77, ceiling at 78, reserve at 80)
is the same as in the placement branch, so the two merge on that hunk.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
